# -- end of source
# `return _this` is how a compiler to ES5 ends every constructor below another. What comes back is proven to be an object, so it is what the construction gives:
# a test that is known to pass, and a join of the object with itself behind it, would give the object a new name, and what the walk knows of the object that it has just made would be lost with the old one.
# RUN: walk f5 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f5:Body
# CHECK-NOT: : true @Boolean = TypeTest
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 29 40 3
# RUN(CALLS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining
# CALLS: 29 40 3
